>
  <h2>Medicare allowed amount</h2>
  <p>
    For a given CPT code and locality, we calculate a reference from the 2026 CMS non-QP Physician Fee
    Schedule. CMS publishes a separate conversion factor for qualifying APM participants, so this is not a
    beneficiary-specific payment estimate. It is a <strong>public reference</strong>, not what every hospital
    charges, what an insurer negotiated, or a coverage decision.
  </p>

  <h2>Fair range heuristic</h2>
  <p>
    Commercial and self-pay prices vary widely. We display an educational range of approximately
    <strong>1.5× to 2.5×</strong> the MPFS reference as an educational comparison heuristic. It is not a
    validated universal fair-market range or a “typical commercial zone.”
  </p>

  <h2>How to interpret results</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Within our range</strong> — a comparison result, not confirmation that the bill is correct</li>
    <li><strong>Above our range</strong> — a reason to ask questions, not proof of overcharging</li>
    <li><strong>Far above our range</strong> — a stronger prompt to review line items and documentation</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Local market, facility fees, emergency settings, and insurance contracts all affect real
    prices. Our benchmarks are starting points for informed questions.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
